    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You recommend books similar to an existing CAP Book.\n\nSource book:\nTitle: {{ $('CAP Book Event').item.json.body.title }}\nDescription: {{ $('CAP Book Event').item.json.body.description }}\nAuthor ID: {{ $('CAP Book Event').item.json.body.authorId }}\nGenre ID: {{ $('CAP Book Event').item.json.body.genreId }}\n\nTask:\nRecommend exactly 3 real, published books that fit the source book’s themes, genre, mood, or likely reader interest.\n\nRules:\n- Do not recommend the source book itself.\n- Make all three recommendations distinct.\n- Prefer a mix of closely related and slightly broader recommendations.\n- Use factual titles, authors, genres, and descriptions. Do not invent books, authors, or links.\n- Each description must be concise.\n- `coverImageUrl` must be a public direct link to a book-cover image, not a webpage, search result, or markdown image.\n- Return only valid JSON. No markdown or text before or after it. \n- The response must conform to the connected output parser. Return JSON only. Do not wrap it in ```json code fences.\n\nReturn this exact shape:\n\n{\n  \"recommendations\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Book title\",\n      \"author\": \"Author name\",\n      \"genre\": \"Readable genre name\",\n      \"description\": \"Short recommendation description and relevance to the source book.\",\n      \"coverImageUrl\": \"https://example.com/book-cover.jpg\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Book title\",\n      \"author\": \"Author name\",\n      \"genre\": \"Readable genre name\",\n      \"description\": \"Short recommendation description and relevance to the source book.\",\n      \"coverImageUrl\": \"https://example.com/book-cover.jpg\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Book title\",\n      \"author\": \"Author name\",\n      \"genre\": \"Readable genre name\",\n      \"description\": \"Short recommendation description and relevance to the source book.\",\n      \"coverImageUrl\": \"https://example.com/book-cover.jpg\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {}
      },
